Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
Upstream-Name: cupertino
Upstream-Contact: Cupertino contributors
Source: https://github.com/orafaelfragoso/cupertino
Comment: The desktop, server and applications are GPL-3+. The toolkit library crates (animation, apps, assets,
 app-protocols, defaults, geometry, icons, keyboard, protocol-app, text-field, theme, typeahead, ui-wayland,
 wayland-client) are MPL-2.0, the protocol description files of the workspace are MIT or Apache-2.0 (the GTK shell
 extension's, from GTK, is LGPL-2.1+), xkbcommon is MIT over the vendored libxkbcommon port (third-party/xkbcommon-rs) and
 the Inter font in the assets crate is OFL-1.1; all are linked into the binaries.
 The licence texts and NOTICE files of the registry crates linked into the binaries are in
 /usr/share/doc/cupertino/THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.
 The LGPL-2.1+, MIT-CMU, BSD-3-Clause and MIT licences below cover protocol description files of registry
 crates that are compiled into the binaries; their copyright notices are in the same file.

